  "response_text": "We subtract the main stack size from the MSP address, so we don\u2019t accidentally cause memory overlap. That new value (MSP minus main stack size) is now the new value for PSP. If we didn\u2019t know the initial value of the MSP, we might accidentally set PSP as some address out of the defined memory space which would cause undefined behaviour. The fact we know MSP allows us to avoid that issue and confidently subtract from the PSP value to create space for a process stack. This method of starting from the \u201cend\u201d of stack space is referred to as \u201cgrowing down\u201d.\\n",
